 and `w+1` columns (3×3 template → period 4 in every pair). The template occupies lattice cell (0,0); a fragment at lattice cell (iy, ix) gets completed there, and further copies are stamped at (iy+sy, ix+sx), (iy+2sy, …) where (sy, sx) are the signs of (iy, ix) — so a fragment directly to the right repeats rightwards (pair 1 colour 4 at (8,15), pair 2 colour 3), one above repeats upwards (pair 1 colour 4 at (5,12): copies at rows 3–5 then rows −1…1, clipped), and a diagonally placed fragment repeats diagonally (pair 3: colour 1 goes down‑right, colour 6 goes up‑right). Partially off‑grid copies are clipped, which explains the odd 4‑cell and 1‑cell pieces at the borders in the fact sheet. The same colour can appear in two different lattice cells (pair 1 colour 4), so fragments are grouped by colour *and* lattice cell.\n\n**Test input.** Template is the 8‑shape at rows 7–9, cols 6–8 (open at the bottom). Colour 2 at column 10 is lattice cell (0,1) → copies at cols 10–12, 14–16, 18–20. Colour 3 at row 11 is lattice cell (1,0) → copies at rows 11–13, 15–17, 19–21 (last one clipped). Colour 4 at (4,10),(5,10) is lattice cell (−1,1) → copy at rows 3–5, cols 10–12, then a clipped copy at rows −1…1, cols 14–16.\n\nThe emit stages follow this construction: for each fragment, first complete it into one full copy, then extend the chain of copies to the border.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    H, W = g.shape\n    bg = background(g)\n    colours = [int(c) for c in np.unique(g) if c != bg]\n    counts = {c: int((g == c).sum()) for c in colours}\n    tc = max(colours, key=lambda c: counts[c])          # template colour = most cells\n\n    tcells = np.argwhere(g == tc)\n    y0, x0 = tcells.min(axis=0)\n    y1, x1 = tcells.max(axis=0)\n    h, w = int(y1 - y0 + 1), int(x1 - x0 + 1)\n    shape = [(int(y - y0), int(x - x0)) for y, x in tcells]\n    py, px = h + 1, w + 1                                # lattice period\n\n    out = g.copy()\n\n    def paint(iy, ix, col):\n        oy, ox = y0 + iy * py, x0 + ix * px\n        hit = False\n        for dy, dx in shape:\n            yy, xx = oy + dy, ox + dx\n            if 0 <= yy < H and 0 <= xx < W:\n                out[yy, xx] = col\n                hit = True\n        return hit\n\n    def sign(v):\n        return (v > 0) - (v < 0)\n\n    for c in colours:\n        if c == tc:\n            continue\n        groups = {}\n        for y, x in np.argwhere(g == c):\n            iy = int((y - y0) // py)\n            ix = int((x - x0) // px)\n            groups.setdefault((iy, ix), []).append((int(y), int(x)))\n        for (iy, ix), cells in groups.items():\n            sy, sx = sign(iy), sign(ix)\n            if sy == 0 and sx == 0:\n                continue\n            paint(iy, ix, c)\n            emit(out.copy(), f\"Complete the colour-{c} fragment at lattice cell ({iy},{ix}) into a full copy of the template shape\")\n            k = 1\n            while paint(iy + k * sy, ix + k * sx, c):\n                k += 1\n            emit(out.copy(), f\"Repeat the colour-{c} copy every ({py},{px}) cells in direction ({sy},{sx}) until it leaves the grid\")\n\n    emit(out.copy(), \"All fragments completed and repeated; final grid\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"repeat":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Where the copies go.** The copies sit on a lattice built from the template: period `h+1` rows and `w+1` columns (3×3 template → period 4 in every pair)."}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The output completes each fragment into a full copy of the template in the fragment's colour, and then repeats that copy further away from the template until it runs off the grid."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Where the copies go.** The copies sit on a lattice built from the template: period `h+1` rows and `w+1` columns (3×3 template → period 4 in every pair)."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"The template occupies lattice cell (0,0); a fragment at lattice cell (iy, ix) gets completed there, and further copies are stamped at (iy+sy, ix+sx), (iy+2sy, …) where (sy, sx) are the signs of (iy, ix) — so a fragment directly to the right repeats rightwards (pair 1 colour 4 at (8,15), pair 2 colour 3), one above repeats upwards (pair 1 colour 4 at (5,12): copies at rows 3–5 then rows −1…1, clipped), and a diagonally placed fragment repeats diag"}],"rays":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"emit stages follow this construction: for each fragment, first complete it into one full copy, then extend the chain of copies to the border."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"3c4fa5d17853672fa134cd3f251328959d532a4b7266c7e7bb5bbeb1de8f37df","task_sha256":"229b1556d22c0aedc0ae43948150dec67808a142703df9a94b8ad079ce89eb53","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
